diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 5c706c3..1f81329 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -33,6 +33,18 @@ nas-convert D:\dir --once                               # foreground, one pass,
 `--start` while a converter runs saves the new job; the running process switches to it **after its
 current file**. No restart needed to reorder folders.

+After each processed file, rescan the active folder (including subfolders with `--recursive`) and
+append newly discovered videos after the existing queue, even after its last file. Completed,
+skipped and failed history stays intact; renamed results are recorded as `output_file` and are not
+new inputs on resume. Saved queue order survives restart; only the initial queue and newly
+discovered batches use largest-first order. Old completed entries infer a missing source's supported
+`.mp4`/`.mkv` result only when exactly one candidate matches `dst_bytes`. Ambiguous candidates stay
+independent inputs. Existing policy retries still apply to an identified result.
+
+Newly appended files must keep the same size and modification time for 5 seconds before processing.
+Changing files remain pending for the next pass; `--once` needs another run for those files. A paused
+copy can look stable, so copy under a temporary non-video extension and rename only when complete.
+
 ## Job model

 | File (in `<dir>`) | Role |
